  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Interior obligated $4.2B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior made 19,068 awards with an average award size of $220K. Obligations fell 35.9% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a peak of $8.1B in FY24 and a decline to $6.5B in FY25 before reaching $4.2B in FY26. Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction is the largest spending category for FY2026 to date at $586M, followed by Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $395M and Computer Systems Design Services at $347M. General Dynamics Information Technology, Inc. leads vendors at $135M, with Ames Federal Contracting Group LLC at $132M and Record Steel and Construction, Inc. at $129M. The Department of the Interior concentrated FY2026 to date spending in construction and IT services, alongside professional services such as Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $185M and Engineering Services at $117M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Interior's contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior obligated $4.2B in FY2026 to date, down 35.9% year over year. Obligations rose from $5.1B in FY21 to $8.1B in FY24, then fell to $6.5B in FY25 and to $4.2B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Interior's biggest procurement categories and vendors right now?",
        "body": "Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction is the largest FY2026 to date category at $586M, followed by Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $395M and Computer Systems Design Services at $347M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the top vendor at $135M, with AMES FEDERAL CONTRACTING GROUP LLC at $132M and RECORD STEEL AND CONSTRUCTION, INC. at $129M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Interior spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Interior obligated $4.2B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior made 19,068 awards with an average award size of $220K. Obligations fell 35.9% year over year and fiscal-year totals show $8.1B in FY24, $6.5B in FY25, and $4.2B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Interior buy?",
      "a": "The Department of the Interior buys a mix of construction, engineering, and IT services. The Department of the Interior spent $586M on Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction, $395M on Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction, $347M on Computer Systems Design Services, $312M on Other Computer Related Services, and $299M on Commercial and Institutional Building Construction, among other categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Interior's largest contractors?",
